From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:13:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Ring and drive Teams calls from the webOS Phone app

Add the webOS front end of the 1:1 Teams calls that teams_calling.c
places and takes (upstream pull request #99), so the stock Phone app
rings, shows and drives them:

- teams_call_luna.c/.h: the com.palm.teams.call luna-service2 service
  the Phone app's CallSynergizer talks to (callStateQuery, dial,
  answer, disconnect, hangupAll, changeMedia; hold, swap, merge,
  extract and DTMF answer true and do nothing). It registers as the
  front end through teams_calling_set_state_cb(),
  teams_calling_set_video_cb() and teams_calling_set_account_cbs(),
  pushes the call's state and video to the subscribers, gives each
  call a card id of its own, clears an ended call's card 1.5 s after
  "disconnected", and tells audiod with CallStatusUpdate when a call
  is active (with "video" for a video call) and when it is over.
- teams_call_video.c/.h: the call's video as the Phone app sees it,
  from the engine's video lines and the offers' video direction: the
  line's incomingVideo/outgoingVideo/incomingVideoState and the
  payload's videoURI and self-view fields. Our own camera's self-view
  is reported while it sends, also before the far side's picture
  comes and while that picture is hidden. tests/test_call_video.c
  covers it; make check runs it.
- libteams.c: register the service at plugin load, not at login. The
  Phone app subscribes to callStateQuery once, when it starts at
  boot, and does not retry a service that was not there. An account
  binds itself through the account hooks when it signs in, which also
  retry a registration that failed at load. Until the service is on
  the bus no front end is registered, so an incoming call is then
  announced as a message, as without a front end.
- Makefile: with TEAMS_CALLING=1, build the two files into
  libteams-personal.so with -DTEAMS_WEBOS_CALL and link luna-service2
  after the objects; stop with an error if pkg-config does not find
  luna-service2, rather than build a plug-in libpurple cannot load.

This replaces the webOS parts of the old layer patches 0012, 0014,
0026, 0027 and 0033, whose calling code is now in #99 (as are the SDP
helpers 0034 added to teams_call_video.c).

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
